From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rzg2l-csi2: skip lane-capability check on RZ/V2H/V2N

rzg2l_validate_csi2_lanes() reads CSI2nMCG.SDLN (offset 0x0, bits 11:8) as
the CSI-2 module's maximum supported data-lane count. That capability
field only exists on RZ/G2L. On RZ/V2H/V2N the CSI-2 uses a different
register layout (the DPHY is programmed via the CRUm_* registers, see
rzv2h_csi2_dphy_enable()), so the read returns bogus bits and the 4-lane
IMX678 is wrongly rejected:

  rzg2l-csi2 16010400.csi21: Failed to support 4 data lanes
  rzg2l-csi2: probe of 16010400.csi21 failed with error -22

The failed probe also leaves a dangling async notifier, which then
crashes the sensor's v4l2_async_register_subdev (v4l2_async_find_match).

Gate the capability read behind a new info flag (has_lane_cap_reg, set
only for RZ/G2L). On RZ/V2H/V2N skip the HW check and trust the
DT-validated lane count (already restricted to 1/2/4). The CSI-2 then
probes and /dev/media0 appears.

Signed-off-by: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-csi2.c b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-csi2.c
index d1935ee62a73..c9751fe908b1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-csi2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/renesas/rzg2l-cru/rzg2l-csi2.c
@@ -142,6 +142,8 @@ struct rzg2l_csi2_info {
 	const struct rzg2l_csi2_format *format;
 	unsigned int num_formats;
 	unsigned int max_width;
+	/* CSI2nMCG.SDLN lane-capability register only exists on RZ/G2L */
+	bool has_lane_cap_reg;
 };
 
 struct rzg2l_csi2_timings {
@@ -544,6 +546,7 @@ static const struct rzg2l_csi2_info rzg2l_csi2_info = {
 	.dphy_enable = rzg2l_csi2_dphy_enable,
 	.dphy_disable = rzg2l_csi2_dphy_disable,
 	.has_system_clk = true,
+	.has_lane_cap_reg = true,
 	.format = rzg2l_csi2_formats,
 	.num_formats = ARRAY_SIZE(rzg2l_csi2_formats),
 	.max_width = 2800,
@@ -995,6 +998,15 @@ static int rzg2l_validate_csi2_lanes(struct rzg2l_csi2 *csi2)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The CSI2nMCG.SDLN lane-capability field only exists on RZ/G2L. On
+	 * RZ/V2H/V2N the CSI-2 uses a different register layout (CRUm_* DPHY
+	 * regs), so this read returns bogus bits and wrongly rejects 4 lanes.
+	 * Skip the HW capability check there and trust the validated DT count.
+	 */
+	if (!csi2->info->has_lane_cap_reg)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(csi2->dev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
